<card id="c" title="Zla Kolata and Prokletije: 300 Euros There and Back">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>The road to Vusanje is mostly asphalt, running through a valley. Bluish mountains on every side, a small river flowing on the right. I stopped by it to rest and cool my feet. Took another break in the shade of a big oak. Along the way I came across cows, and sometimes sheep and donkeys. It all looked like the beginning of The Lord of the Rings.</p>
<p>A little over an hour of easy walking, and at around 15:00 I was at the <a href="https://www.guesthousededushi.com/">campsite</a>.</p>
<p>The campsite pleasantly surprised me. On its grounds there are several guest houses and two levels of tent pitches. There are two showers with hot water, two toilets, a dishwashing area and an outdoor kitchen. The owners&apos; house is there too, so they&apos;re on site around the clock.</p>
